## Resolve a pronoun target, never refuse it

Applies to every skill that takes a target in `$ARGUMENTS`: assess, verify, implement,
fix-issue, cover, review-pr.

**Detect.** Strip the flags (`--model=`, `--effort=`, `--tier=` and the like). The target
needs resolving when what is left is a bare pronoun or deictic: `them`, `this`, `that`,
`these`, `those`, `it`, `they`, `same`, `the above`, `the last one`, `that one`,
`what we just did`. An empty target needs resolving only when the skill has no default
for it (review-pr with no argument reviews the current branch's PR; that default stands).

**Refusing is the bug, not the safe option.** Measured 2026-08-28: `/ork:assess them`
was sent one message after "bug in orchestkit hooks", mid-investigation of
`pretool/bash/dangerous-command-blocker`, and the skill replied that "them" had "no
antecedent anywhere in this conversation". It had two (#3780).

### Inline skills (the body runs in the main thread)

1. Read back for the NEAREST concrete subject: a file just discussed, a diff or PR just
   opened, a component just investigated, an issue just named.
2. Announce the resolution in one line, then proceed with it as the target:
   *"Reading 'them' as the 3 pretool guards we just probed; say otherwise and I'll switch."*
   A wrong guess then costs one correction instead of a turn.
3. Ask only when the conversation is genuinely empty (a fresh session that opens with a
   bare pronoun). That is the one case with nothing to read back to.

### Forked skills (`context: fork`, the body runs in a subagent)

A fork cannot see the conversation, so it cannot read back. Check the target FIRST,
before any probe, Agent or Workflow call. If it needs resolving, return exactly this
one line and nothing else, then stop:

```
TARGET_UNRESOLVED: <word>
```

`<word>` is the pronoun as typed (`this`, `them`), or `(empty)`.

### The caller (main thread) on a TARGET_UNRESOLVED result

The main thread has the conversation. Do not relay the sentinel to the user, and do not
ask what the pronoun means. Resolve `<word>` as in the inline half (nearest concrete
subject), announce the resolution in one line, and invoke the same skill again with the
concrete target and the original flags. Ask only when the conversation is empty. Since
CC 2.1.218 a fork may run in the background, so the sentinel can arrive as a task
notification; act on it the same way.
